@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Process an amendment or cancellation — End-to-end interaction
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Accommodation Provider Agent" as Actor
participant "Provider Portal / PMS" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Provider Integration Adapter" as Edge
participant "Booking.com Distribution Channel" as Service1
participant "Provider PMS / Channel Manager" as Service2
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events
participant "Booking.com Demand API" as BookingCom #FBDADD


group 1. Deliver a confirmed supplier reservation into the provider channel.
  Actor -> Surface: Deliver a confirmed supplier reservation into the provider channel
  Surface -> Gateway: EVENT booking.reservation.created.v1
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Deliver a confirmed supplier reservation into the provider channel.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Booking.com Distribution Channel data
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Apply or reject an amendment/cancellation and return commercial impact.
  Actor -> Surface: Apply or reject an amendment/cancellation and return commercial impact
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /provider-api/v1/reservations/{reservationId}/changes
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service2: Apply or reject an amendment/cancellation and return commercial impact.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service2 -> Service2: Validate transition and persist
  Service2 -> BookingCom: distribution channel
  BookingCom --> Service2: Supplier response + request_id
  Service2 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service2 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service2 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
